          "owner_id": "own_1177056",
          "prev_trainers": [],
          "prev_owners": [],
          "comment": "Impressive in the Royal Hunt Cup but these terms do demand a further spike in his form",
          "spotlight": "Half-brother to top miler Palace Pier; slow burner who has won his last four and justified heaps of market confidence when showing a smart turn of foot up the stands' rail to see off his 29 rivals in the Royal Hunt Cup (1m, good to firm); smacked of a Group horse that day but these terms do demand a further spike in his form.",
          "quotes": [
            {
              "date": "2025-06-18",
              "horse": "My Cloud",
              "horse_id": "hrs_39147976",
              "race": "Royal Hunt Cup (Heritage Handicap)",
              "race_id": "rac_11622819",
              "course": "Ascot",
              "course_id": "crs_52",
              "distance_f": "8",
              "distance_y": "1760",
              "quote": "I was just so pleased to be sat on a nice horse like My Cloud. You have to keep an eye on the whole race, drawn 32 but I have to look over the whole field with my eyes. He pleased me every furlong, I take him back and he wants to go forward and I could see Christophe [Soumillon, jockey on the fourth] travelled well and I'd say he opened the gaps for me but he's such a nice horse and he deserved this. He's a nice horse, he'll go places. I'd like to see him [kept] over a mile at the moment - Silvestre De Sousa, jockey."
            }
          ],
          "stable_tour": [
            {
              "quote": "Hopefully, he creeps in at the bottom of the weights and I don't think I'd swap him if he does. He's a horse on the up, which is what you need in these sorts of races, and I've been thinking about this race for a long time. We've always rated him highly and he should enjoy the Hunt Cup test. Good to firm ground would be ideal. 09-06-25"
            }
          ],
