          "comment": "A winner in May but last in his final two runs and back to the drawing board",
          "spotlight": "Not had lots of racing and things were looking up when edging out a useful yardstick at Doncaster in May (1m6f, good to firm), only to then not beat a rival in his next two races (1m5f/2m); back to the drawing board.",
          "quotes": [],
          "stable_tour": [
            {
              "quote": "He's a frustrating horse. He would not go around the bend at Goodwood last time out. He's so straightforward at home but it's like something switches when he goes to the racecourse. He becomes tricky but he's a talented horse who wants to stay and that's his game. I'll probably keep him busy this autumn and get him racing regularly to teach him how to race. I think a mile and a half is ideal and as long as there are no extremes in the ground I think he'll be fine anywhere in the middle. 04-09-24"
            }
          ],
