          "comment": "Peak Flat and hurdle form respected; soft ground perhaps not ideal at Chester latest",
          "spotlight": "Very capable off this sort of mark when with Sir Mark Prescott; won three of his four hurdle starts for current yard and was returning from a long break (and wind surgery) when beaten 16l at Chester (soft); handles that surface but probably happier under these conditions; certainly not ruled out.",
          "quotes": [
            {
              "date": "2024-08-31",
              "horse": "Brave Knight",
              "horse_id": "hrs_28013104",
              "race": "Newton Abbot Racecourse On Facebook Novices' Hurdle (GBB Race)",
              "race_id": "rac_11358295",
              "course": "Newton Abbot",
              "course_id": "crs_1014",
              "distance_f": "17",
              "distance_y": "3687",
              "quote": "We had Brave Knight in the autumn after he'd run on the Flat and I don't know whether he was a tad jarred up from running in the summer, but he couldn't jump at all. We sent him home, reschooled him, and he's a totally different animal now he's had a bit of time and he jumps enthusiastically. There's a 70 grand race at Worcester on September 27 and he had to have a third run to have qualified for that, so that's where he'll go next I suspect -  Trainer Paul Nicholls, speaking on Sky Sports Racing."
            }
          ],
          "stable_tour": [
            {
              "quote": "He was up in grade when weakening up the hill at Cheltenham last month. We're having his palate re-cauterised and he'll be back in the spring. With his preference for good ground, he's more of a spring-summer horse. 04-11-24"
            }
          ],
