          "owner_id": "own_1252280",
          "prev_trainers": [],
          "prev_owners": [],
          "comment": "Fine course record and ran a cracker in the Wokingham; stall 1 a potential stumbling block",
          "spotlight": "Progressive last year, with his three wins including two at Ascot (one over C&D); confirmed his affinity for the track with a good fourth in the Wokingham three weeks ago, a race where he was finishing fast up the stands' rail and comfortably beating the others to race on that part of the track; 1lb rise manageable but with the stalls on the stands' side there must be a query over the suitability of stall 1.",
          "quotes": [
            {
              "date": "2024-10-04",
              "horse": "Holkham Bay",
              "horse_id": "hrs_28532917",
              "race": "BetMGM Handicap",
              "race_id": "rac_11386180",
              "course": "Ascot",
              "course_id": "crs_52",
              "distance_f": "6",
              "distance_y": "1320",
              "quote": "I'm delighted and the little bit of juice in the ground helped Holkham Bay, as it was quick enough at Doncaster last time. We'll put him away now but we'll be looking forward to next year, and we hope he can be a nice horse for the big Saturday TV races. He loves Ascot and we'll definitely be looking towards June next year, especially if there's some juice in the ground, but for now he's earned a well-deserved holiday - William Knight, trainer."
            },
            {
              "date": "2024-08-10",
              "horse": "Holkham Bay",
              "horse_id": "hrs_28532917",
              "race": "Dubai Duty Free Shergar Cup Dash (Handicap)",
              "race_id": "rac_11338886",
              "course": "Ascot",
              "course_id": "crs_52",
              "distance_f": "5",
              "distance_y": "1100",
              "quote": "The owners have been telling me for about three months that the Portland at Doncaster is his race, and they could be right. I think Holkham Bay is a premium sprinter but the key is a flat course and a strong pace. There is a race at York on the final day of the Ebor in two weeks that we are considering on the way to Doncaster - William Knight, trainer."
            }
          ],
          "stable_tour": [
            {
              "quote": "He had been pleasing me before his debut at Lingfield this month and ran a lovely race to finish second over 6f. We'll try to win a novice back at Lingfield in the next fortnight. Further down the line there are some sales races we may look at. 30-06-22"
            }
          ],
