          "comment": "Below par in two outings in the spring but was a Listed winner for previous yard",
          "spotlight": "C&D winner who made good progress over 7f for Tom Clover once cheekpieces were fitted, including a ready Listed win at Newbury (soft) last autumn; below that level in two starts for new stable but could play a leading role if back to anywhere near his best after 105 days off.",
          "quotes": [
            {
              "date": "2024-09-20",
              "horse": "Witness Stand",
              "horse_id": "hrs_35149667",
              "race": "Dubai Duty Free Cup Stakes (Listed Race)",
              "race_id": "rac_11373960",
              "course": "Newbury",
              "course_id": "crs_936",
              "distance_f": "7",
              "distance_y": "1540",
              "quote": "Witness Stand's last two runs had been career bests and this was another big step up. He's not overly big but he has a big heart and is versatile regarding conditions - Kieran Shoemark, jockey."
            }
          ],
          "stable_tour": [
            {
              "quote": "The son of Expert Eye looks the part. He has done all we had been asking of him at home and we gave him his first run at Chester last Friday, where I thought it would take a nice one to beat him, and he proved me right with a very professional performance in winning on his debut. Danny brought him off the rail as they entered the short straight and in a matter of strides the race was over. I could not be happier with him, and we will wait and see how he recovers from his first day at the races before making any decisions. We are in no rush as I think he has a lovely future. 06-07-23"
            }
          ],
