          "comment": "Unexposed filly; good win at York last month and a solid effort against her elders latest",
          "spotlight": "Lightly raced filly who dig deep to win a 6f handicap (good to firm) at York last month; solid fourth at Thirsk ten days ago, a race where she got messed about a bit, and she's still capable of better; well drawn provided she breaks on terms.",
          "quotes": [
            {
              "date": "2025-06-13",
              "horse": "Easy Peeler",
              "horse_id": "hrs_40919767",
              "race": "British EBF Supporting Racing With Pride Fillies' Handicap",
              "race_id": "rac_11637457",
              "course": "York",
              "course_id": "crs_2782",
              "distance_f": "6",
              "distance_y": "1320",
              "quote": "My gut feeling is Easy Peeler won't come back tomorrow as she doesn't need to. She's won a good race on a very warm day, and got warm before the race and has expended a lot of energy. She's a filly we like and her and the winner have pulled clear. She's progressing nicely and there's loads of handicaps to go for. Whitsbury Manor have leased her to Hot To Trot and she'll be a broodmare there eventually, so they'd love to get black type, but that's a little bit away from our minds at the moment -  Sean Quinn, joint-trainer."
            }
          ],
          "stable_tour": [
            {
              "quote": "She's a lovely half-sister to Apeeling and the Quinns have always liked her. She got the job done at Catterick last week despite the track not being ideal. We'll probably run her again under a penalty before possibly raising our sights. It's handy that she can start off at a low level but she's definitely got lots of potential. 02-08-24"
            }
          ],
