          "prev_trainers": [],
          "prev_owners": [],
          "comment": "Has penalty for Ayr win on Monday but was as good as ever with that success; big player",
          "spotlight": "4yo who recorded her fourth win when justifying support at Ayr (6f, good to soft) on Monday; this is tougher under a penalty but she was as good as ever last time and is versatile ground-wise; key player for in-form yard.",
          "quotes": [
            {
              "date": "2025-07-07",
              "horse": "Taygar",
              "horse_id": "hrs_34473586",
              "race": "Start Your Racing TV Free Trial Handicap (Div II)",
              "race_id": "rac_11692174",
              "course": "Ayr",
              "course_id": "crs_78",
              "distance_f": "6",
              "distance_y": "1320",
              "quote": "Taygar is tricky. She goes down early but she goes when she wants to go! She's not easy at all but she's got ability and she's just been waiting for some soft ground. Things didn't really go to plan but once Danny [Tudhope] got out she dropped her head a bit and settled well but, because of that, he had to send her on earlier than he would have liked. To be fair to her, she kept going and she's done it well - Michael Dods, trainer, speaking to Racing TV."
            }
          ],
          "stable_tour": [
            {
              "quote": "I haven't done too much with my 2yos but this filly actually won first time out for us back in April. I don't usually have many youngsters out at that time of the year but she was showing a lot of speed and won well. Her next run at Pontefract was a different story as she was too keen and gave herself no chance, while at Redcar last time out she encountered good to firm ground for the first time and although she ran well, I felt she would appreciate a little more cut. We will look to upping her in trip to 6f next and find some slower ground. 26-07-23"
            }
          ],
