          "comment": "Mixed record in Ireland this year and out of sorts in last three runs; others preferred",
          "spotlight": "Nine-time winner, including two over C&D; well handicapped on best form last season but has mixed record in Ireland this year and she's been out of sorts in last three runs; has questions to answer and she wouldn't want the ground to dry out.",
          "quotes": [
            {
              "date": "2024-04-29",
              "horse": "Catherine Chroi",
              "horse_id": "hrs_21678216",
              "race": "Virgin Bet Daily Extra Places Apprentice Handicap",
              "race_id": "rac_11237850",
              "course": "Ayr",
              "course_id": "crs_78",
              "distance_f": "6",
              "distance_y": "1320",
              "quote": "Catherine Chroi is a tough little filly and very consistent. She rarely runs a bad race so hopefully she can go out and win again at some point. It's harder to win in Ireland than it is here, but she enjoys being trained with us and we're picking the right type of races for her. She's thriving - Iain Jardine, trainer."
            }
          ],
          "stable_tour": [
            {
              "quote": "She's thriving and I hope she can stay on an upward curve. She was rated 41 when she joined us and she's won six times and shot right up to 75. But I still think she can win off her new mark. She's getting stronger and ran well in a good race at Ayr last time, doing her best work at the end. The Bronze Cup at that venue could be a good target. She needs a wee bit of give in the ground and if there's no pace she has to go on herself. 26-07-24"
            }
          ],
