          "comment": "Nine wins on turf; runner-up at Musselburgh latest but drying ground wouldn't be ideal",
          "spotlight": "All of his nine wins have been on good or slower, including four over C&D; made a slow start to this season but he returned to form with a close second at Musselburgh (1m1f, good) 11 days ago; has claims if he can back that up but drying ground wouldn't be ideal.",
          "quotes": [],
          "stable_tour": [
            {
              "quote": "He joined us in the spring still a maiden after 25 runs, but he's really come alive since arriving here. I'd like to take all the credit but he's ridden by 74-year-old Jack Grey, who has done an amazing job. Jack has found the key to him and he has gone from strength to strength, winning five times and charging up the handicap from 47 to 69. Paul [Mulrennan] had ridden him before and told me he was much better than his form and he could be having a problem with his breathing, and a wind operation has clearly helped him. He's showing no signs of either regression or tiredness and, while he's in that form, I have every hope he can add another win very soon. 12-09-22"
            }
          ],
