          "prev_trainers": [],
          "prev_owners": [],
          "comment": "Went close in 2yo Group 3 last September; hasn't kicked on during 3yo campaign",
          "spotlight": "Went close in Group 3 Firth Of Clyde Stakes at Ayr (6f, good to firm) last September; reappeared with fair fifth of 15 in the Group 3 Fred Darling at Newbury (7f, good) in April but has failed to build on that and she needs to raise her game now back up in trip.",
          "quotes": [
            {
              "date": "2024-06-19",
              "horse": "Maw Lam",
              "horse_id": "hrs_41189806",
              "race": "Queen Mary Stakes (Group 2) (Fillies)",
              "race_id": "rac_11299392",
              "course": "Ascot",
              "course_id": "crs_52",
              "distance_f": "5",
              "distance_y": "1100",
              "quote": "I'm delighted. Obviously Maw Lam was very unlucky the last day. They went fast, Hollie said, and she finished strong, so to get black type in the Queen Mary is brilliant. We'll see what the team want to do - hopefully go for a Listed race, then onwards to better things, hopefully. She's very, very relaxed. She likes the attention. She was asleep 20 minutes before the girls went to put the bridle on her, which stands her in good stead, so hopefully now maybe France, there's a race in Ireland. Let her stop blowing, and then make a decision - Adrian Nicholls, trainer."
            }
          ],
          "stable_tour": [
            {
              "quote": "She's a smart filly. She's shown that in all her runs and I was delighted with her performances at Royal Ascot and Newmarket. Her owner, Chris Hirst, came to the yard last year and she cost a few quid as a yearling, but she's always shown a lot of class. She won on her debut at Thirsk and then everything that could go wrong went wrong at Beverley. We were confident of a good run at Ascot and arguably, again with a better run through, she could have been second. The Duchess of Cambridge Stakes at Newmarket on Friday was a really hot race and it was a very good run to be beaten just under three lengths in a Group 2. I think she got the 6f trip and she has the speed for 5f as well. She's very exciting and it's onwards and upwards for her. 26-07-24"
            }
          ],
