          "prev_trainers": [],
          "prev_owners": [],
          "comment": "Won first two after a gelding op and first home in his group in Britannia since; claims",
          "spotlight": "Expensive to follow at two but returned from a gelding operation to win an AW maiden and followed up in the Esher Cup at Sandown (1m, good) on handicap debut later in April; first home in his group when seventh of 30 in the Britannia at Royal Ascot (1m, good to firm) since, suggesting his mark could still be very workable; the first-time cheekpieces he wore at Ascot are retained.",
          "quotes": [
            {
              "date": "2025-04-25",
              "horse": "Fifth Column",
              "horse_id": "hrs_42452095",
              "race": "bet365 Esher Cup Handicap",
              "race_id": "rac_11589318",
              "course": "Sandown",
              "course_id": "crs_1404",
              "distance_f": "8",
              "distance_y": "1760",
              "quote": "Gelding has calmed Fifth Column down and made him a happier horse. Having had a run and won on the all-weather he was fully race fit, which he needed to be as the ground was slow, which is quite correct with there being jumpers here tomorrow. He had been working well at home and I thought if we had a winner today it would be in this race. We'll stay at a mile and aim for the Britannia at Royal Ascot and hope we get drawn on the right side. He could run before if we need to freshen him and can find the right spot; he will tell me - John Gosden, joint-trainer."
            },
            {
              "date": "2025-04-07",
              "horse": "Fifth Column",
              "horse_id": "hrs_42452095",
              "race": "Try Unibet's New Improved Acca Boosts Maiden Stakes (GBB Race) (Div II)",
              "race_id": "rac_11601161",
              "course": "Kempton (AW)",
              "course_id": "crs_28054",
              "distance_f": "8",
              "distance_y": "1760",
              "quote": "We didn't go overly quick and I was trapped a couple of rows further back than ideal. Fifth Column showed a good turn of foot stepping up to the mile for the first time and he hit the line well. A mile is probably his optimal trip and we'll see where he goes from here - Kieren Shoemark, jockey, speaking to Racing TV."
            }
          ],
