          "prev_owners": [
            {
              "owner": "The Rogues Gallery",
              "owner_id": "own_1170212",
              "change_date": "2024-04-30"
            }
          ],
          "comment": "Globetrotting of late; faces a stiffer assignment returned to home soil",
          "spotlight": "Has shown very useful form on home soil and internationally, including a success in Qatar and close second in US Grade 2 this year; below par last time and faces a stiffer assignment on this return to British racing; gained last domestic win in 2023.",
          "quotes": [
            {
              "date": "2025-04-08",
              "horse": "Rogue Lightning",
              "horse_id": "hrs_30765182",
              "race": "Valvoline Global Shakertown Stakes (Grade 2) (3yo+) (Turf)",
              "race_id": "rac_11599029",
              "course": "Keeneland",
              "course_id": "crs_7826",
              "distance_f": "5.5",
              "distance_y": "1210",
              "quote": "Rogue Lightning ran a great race He was always up there and led in the straight but was just run out of it. He's lost nothing in defeat and I feel we'll leave him out there to run in another Grade 2 sprint at Churchill Downs over Kentucky Derby weekend [May 3]. If you look at it another way, he would have had to carry a penalty in that if he'd won at Keeneland, so it could work in our favour - Tom Clover, trainer."
            },
            {
              "date": "2025-02-16",
              "horse": "Rogue Lightning",
              "horse_id": "hrs_30765182",
              "race": "Dukhan Sprint (Local Group 3) (3yo+) (Turf)",
              "race_id": "rac_11544585",
              "course": "Al Uqda",
              "course_id": "crs_43992",
              "distance_f": "6",
              "distance_y": "1320",
              "quote": "That was marvellous. Mickael [Barzalona, jockey] did well to drop Rogue Lightning out early from his draw and everything went well. He came through the horses smoothly - Tom Clover, trainer."
            },
            {
              "date": "2023-09-17",
              "horse": "Rogue Lightning",
              "horse_id": "hrs_30765182",
              "race": "Betfred Scarbrough Stakes (Listed Race)",
              "race_id": "rac_11019658",
              "course": "Doncaster",
              "course_id": "crs_390",
              "distance_f": "5",
              "distance_y": "1103",
              "quote": "We put Rogue Lightning in the Abbaye and if he's okay we'll go there. I've always really liked him and he's very fast - Tom Clover, trainer."
            },
            {
              "date": "2023-08-12",
              "horse": "Rogue Lightning",
              "horse_id": "hrs_30765182",
              "race": "Dubai Duty Free Shergar Cup Dash (Handicap)",
              "race_id": "rac_10987470",
              "course": "Ascot",
              "course_id": "crs_52",
              "distance_f": "5",
              "distance_y": "1100",
              "quote": "Rogue Lightning is a really nice horse and it was very sporting of the owners to come to a race like this. I think we'll perhaps look at something like the Scarborough Stakes at Doncaster next. He won well there last time and hopefully looks like he's worth a crack at stakes company now. He showed plenty of talent as a 2yo but bringing him back to 5f with a hood has really helped and he's relaxed and grown up - Tom Clover, trainer."
            },
            {
              "date": "2023-07-07",
              "horse": "Rogue Lightning",
              "horse_id": "hrs_30765182",
              "race": "Samantha Glendinning Takepayments Handicap",
              "race_id": "rac_10960222",
              "course": "Doncaster",
              "course_id": "crs_390",
              "distance_f": "5",
              "distance_y": "1103",
              "quote": "Gelding him, applying the hood and and the drop back to five furlongs seems to have helped him just relax a bit. Carrie Browning rides him every day and she also rides Rogue Millennium. She's got him back fit and deserves a lot of the credit. Rogue Lightning has always been a horse with lots of ability and it's nice to see him show some of his full potential today - Tom Clover, trainer."
            }
          ],
          "stable_tour": [
            {
              "quote": "He got back from America last week. It was great for him to win in Qatar given his connections and then he ran a huge race at Keeneland. It didn't work out for us at Churchill Downs last time. He was caught wide and they'd had a lot of rain, so he had a bit of wheelspin and it was really hard to make up ground there. We need to put a line through it and go again. I want to enter him in the July Cup. I feel like 6f is what he wants now and hopefully he can still fly the flag for us this year. 14-05-25"
            }
          ],
