          "comment": "Solid results over 6f this term; this 3yo may still rate higher; not dismissed",
          "spotlight": "Very useful form, mostly over 5f, last season; solid results over 6f this term, winning at Ascot (Group 3) then not disgraced at Haydock (Group 2) or Royal Ascot (Commonwealth Cup); ties in with fellow 3yos Symbol Of Honour and Whistlejacket; may still rate higher and can't be dismissed.",
          "quotes": [
            {
              "date": "2025-04-30",
              "horse": "Big Mojo",
              "horse_id": "hrs_42554183",
              "race": "eventmasters.co.uk Commonwealth Cup Trial Stakes (Group 3) (Registered As The Pavilion Stakes)",
              "race_id": "rac_11590384",
              "course": "Ascot",
              "course_id": "crs_52",
              "distance_f": "6",
              "distance_y": "1320",
              "quote": "I'd think the King Charles would be more likely. Training on is always a concern if you've got a decent two-year-old, but at home Big Mojo had been showing us he had. He's been working really well against some of the older horses - Mick Appleby, trainer."
            },
            {
              "date": "2024-07-31",
              "horse": "Big Mojo",
              "horse_id": "hrs_42554183",
              "race": "Jaeger-Lecoultre Molecomb Stakes (Group 3)",
              "race_id": "rac_11335870",
              "course": "Goodwood",
              "course_id": "crs_546",
              "distance_f": "5",
              "distance_y": "1100",
              "quote": "It's great, Big Mojo is an exciting horse and he's improved a lot since his debut. It's a nice way to break a maiden, in a Group 3 race, and he's a pro horse. He's only going to improve. He's got a lot of speed and I like him over six as well. He's a quality horse going forward, he's strong physically but mentally he's not there yet - Silvestre de Sousa, rider."
            }
          ],
