          "comment": "Has an impressive record (161111) over 6f and may well improve further; big player",
          "spotlight": "Stablemate of Notable Speech; suited by good/firmer; has a very impressive record (161111) over 6f, narrowly justifying favouritism in the Sandy Lane Stakes (Group 2) at Haydock most recently; beat Ides Of March at Newbury (Listed) a week earlier; unable to run in the Commonwealth Cup due to being a gelding; major contender, with further improvement plausible kept to this trip and back from a well-earned break (had a busy May).",
          "quotes": [
            {
              "date": "2025-05-24",
              "horse": "Symbol Of Honour",
              "horse_id": "hrs_39960459",
              "race": "Betfred Sandy Lane Stakes (Group 2)",
              "race_id": "rac_11620076",
              "course": "Haydock",
              "course_id": "crs_598",
              "distance_f": "6",
              "distance_y": "1320",
              "quote": "Symbol Of Honour toughed it and showed a good attitude. I don't think he was quite the same horse as he was last week, but you can't fault him. I've just spoken to Charlie [Appleby] and we might give him a break now. He was in Dubai over the winter and ultimately he's probably a horse to go back there. We'll see where we go between now and then - Alex Merriam, assistant trainer."
            },
            {
              "date": "2025-05-17",
              "horse": "Symbol Of Honour",
              "horse_id": "hrs_39960459",
              "race": "Highclere Castle Gin Carnarvon Stakes (Listed Race)",
              "race_id": "rac_11606387",
              "course": "Newbury",
              "course_id": "crs_936",
              "distance_f": "6",
              "distance_y": "1320",
              "quote": "Dropping back to six furlongs has been the making of Symbol Of Honour. Physically and mentally he's doing well but where we go now I'm not sure. He's not a horse for the Jersey Stakes [over seven furlongs] because I don't think he saw that trip out last time. He's a strong traveller and it's good to get him back on track - Charlie Appleby, trainer."
            },
            {
              "date": "2025-01-10",
              "horse": "Symbol Of Honour",
              "horse_id": "hrs_39960459",
              "race": "Al Wasl Stakes Sponsored By DP World (Conditions) (Turf)",
              "race_id": "rac_11514945",
              "course": "Meydan",
              "course_id": "crs_32006",
              "distance_f": "6",
              "distance_y": "1320",
              "quote": "Symbol Of Honour had to dig really deep. I think he probably needed the race after a bit of a layoff but I really liked that when he got headed he battled back gamely. The five and six furlong races here, when they meet the intersection and the straight course, the race really starts and we just got caught a little flat-footed there. I think he's more a horse for six-seven furlongs, he's not a horse to drop down in distance - William Buick, jockey."
            }
          ],
