          "comment": "Made all in the Thirsk Hunt Cup then perhaps unsuited by the track at Epsom last time",
          "spotlight": "Flopped at Epsom last month (first visit) but was perhaps unsuited by the tricky track; prior to that he made all in the Thirsk Hunt Cup (1m, good) and is just 3lb higher today; could bounce back with a bold bid.",
          "quotes": [],
          "stable_tour": [
            {
              "quote": "His season fell apart last term but he's had an operation to remove one of his testicles and is moving much better as a result. He's definitely working like he's back to his best and I'm confident he can bounce back. If the ground is decent, he'll probably go to Thirsk on Saturday for a seven-furlong conditions race and then maybe something like the Royal Hunt Cup. 11-04-25"
            },
            {
              "quote": "He's a lovely colt who won on the second of his two runs last year at Newcastle in November. He strengthened up nicely over the winter and I was happy enough with his run back, again at Gosforth Park when a neck second a Listed race over a mile. He goes to the 2,000 Guineas on Saturday where the bare form is not good enough. However, he will step forward hugely for having that run under his belt as he lost 15kg last time out which is a big amount for any race. He worked very well under Danny Tudhope last week and he will go well. 07-05-23"
            }
          ],
