          "prev_trainers": [],
          "prev_owners": [
            {
              "owner": "Clipper Logistics",
              "owner_id": "own_629448",
              "change_date": "2025-03-26"
            }
          ],
          "comment": "Made it 4-8 with C&D win in May & this progressive 4yo could still be ahead of handicapper",
          "spotlight": "4yo who made it 4-8, and 2-2 at York, when scoring over C&D (good to firm) in May on his first run beyond about 1m; a 4lb rise isn't harsh and this progressive sort could still be ahead of the handicapper.",
          "quotes": [
            {
              "date": "2025-05-16",
              "horse": "Thunder Run",
              "horse_id": "hrs_41814780",
              "race": "Knights Solicitors Handicap (GBBPlus Race)",
              "race_id": "rac_11605997",
              "course": "York",
              "course_id": "crs_2782",
              "distance_f": "10.5",
              "distance_y": "2256",
              "quote": "Thunder Run loves the track, but the step up in trip was the key. He needed to relax but after half a furlong he took off with Clifford [Lee] - the last thing I said to him was do not make it. I'd have dragged him off coming back in if he did!  Once he got a bit of cover he got him in a lovely rhythm. I didn't want him to hit the front too soon but didn't think it'd be that late. It nearly gave me a heart attack.  When he learns to race a bit more economically he's definitely a Listed or Group 3 horse. The Wolferton at Royal Ascot will be the plan. His new owners paid a nice bit of money for him before the Lincoln and they'd love to have a runner there - Karl Burke, trainer."
            },
            {
              "date": "2024-08-22",
              "horse": "Thunder Run",
              "horse_id": "hrs_41814780",
              "race": "Clipper Handicap (Heritage Handicap)",
              "race_id": "rac_11328473",
              "course": "York",
              "course_id": "crs_2782",
              "distance_f": "8",
              "distance_y": "1732",
              "quote": "Thunder Run is still very raw and it wasn't the plan to go out and make it, but David (Egan) said he jumped out very well as they didn't feel they were going quick enough. But if something took him it probably would've cost him the race - he was on fresh air for the last 100 yards. We only ran Thunder Run at Thirsk last time as he needed a penalty to get in. Thank god he didn't win, because he might've got beat with a 6lb penalty - Karl Burke, trainer."
            },
            {
              "date": "2024-07-03",
              "horse": "Thunder Run",
              "horse_id": "hrs_41814780",
              "race": "British EBF Novice Stakes (GBB Race)",
              "race_id": "rac_11314121",
              "course": "Thirsk",
              "course_id": "crs_2080",
              "distance_f": "8",
              "distance_y": "1758",
              "quote": "Thunder Run was entitled to improve a lot from his first run. We had loads of excuses at Wetherby, he was slow away and drawn wide, and William's (Haggas)  horse got the run of the race. I felt we were unlucky not to win. He's quite a relaxed horse and he quickened up well when Danny asked him. I'd say it was a good performance and he's a smart horse. Danny likes him and I'd say we can go upwards from here - Karl Burke, trainer."
            }
          ],
          "stable_tour": [
            {
              "quote": "He ended up having to do the donkey work on his return in the Lincoln and just got tired late on but he showed the benefit of that run in winning at York when stepping up in trip last time. I've always thought he'll make up into a Group horse and the Wolferton looks an ideal next step. 12-06-25"
            }
          ],
