          "comment": "Sixth of 30 in Royal Hunt Cup last month and could have more to offer now back up in trip",
          "spotlight": "Won over 1m2f for Sir Michael Stoute and scored in style on his stable and seasonal debut at Newmarket (1m1f, good) in May; first home in the centre group when sixth of 30 in the Royal Hunt Cup (1m, good to firm) last month and he could have more to offer now back up in trip; interesting contender for connections who won this in 2019 and 2021.",
          "quotes": [
            {
              "date": "2025-05-03",
              "horse": "Fox Legacy",
              "horse_id": "hrs_36779897",
              "race": "Betfred Suffolk Stakes (Heritage Handicap)",
              "race_id": "rac_11575603",
              "course": "Newmarket",
              "course_id": "crs_988",
              "distance_f": "9",
              "distance_y": "1980",
              "quote": "Fox Legacy had been working well at home and this was a good starting point for him. I believe Sir Michael [Stoute, former trainer] had always liked him and his horses were always bought to develop and improve with time and we're lucky to have him. He could possibly be one for the Royal Ascot team. He is a handicapper and has won off 90, so we will look at our options - Andrew Balding, trainer."
            }
          ],
