          "comment": "In good form in the second half of spring; may not have been suited by Epsom last time",
          "spotlight": "Won at Ripon (1m2f, good) in April then placed the next twice, on the first occasion third to Thunder Run over this C&D (good to firm); slowly away and perhaps unsuited by Epsom when well beaten last time; each-way contender if back on song this afternoon.",
          "quotes": [
            {
              "date": "2023-08-03",
              "horse": "Have Secret",
              "horse_id": "hrs_30314669",
              "race": "Coral Kincsem Handicap",
              "race_id": "rac_10984129",
              "course": "Goodwood",
              "course_id": "crs_546",
              "distance_f": "10",
              "distance_y": "2177",
              "quote": "Have Secret has run a cracking race, which he has done all season. He's a horse who is getting better with racing, but he keeps just finding one or two. But we are delighted with him - Richard Fahey, trainer."
            },
            {
              "date": "2022-10-05",
              "horse": "Have Secret",
              "horse_id": "hrs_30314669",
              "race": "British Stallion Studs EBF Nursery Handicap",
              "race_id": "rac_10668567",
              "course": "Nottingham",
              "course_id": "crs_1040",
              "distance_f": "10",
              "distance_y": "2250",
              "quote": "Have Secret tends to race behind the bridle but keeps finding. The step up in trip helped him and he handled the ground. Oisin Orr, jockey."
            },
            {
              "date": "2022-08-07",
              "horse": "Have Secret",
              "horse_id": "hrs_30314669",
              "race": "Sky Bet Sunday Series Nursery Handicap",
              "race_id": "rac_10618283",
              "course": "Haydock",
              "course_id": "crs_598",
              "distance_f": "7",
              "distance_y": "1532",
              "quote": "Have Secret deserved that after he ran well at Chester last week on a course that didn't suit him. He was going to go up the ratings so we thought we'd come here and he's going to go up even further now. He'll make a nice 3yo next year - Robin O'Ryan, assistant to trainer Richard Fahey."
            }
          ],
