          "comment": "Unlucky second at Newcastle last time; unexposed at the trip and could have a part to play",
          "spotlight": "Ex-French 4yo who has raced only six times; ran well on first two stable starts (including over 1m here on fast ground) and bounced back from Redcar flop with close second at Newcastle (1m2f, AW), where he may well have won with a clear run; unexposed at the trip and could have a part to play.",
          "quotes": [
            {
              "date": "2025-04-21",
              "horse": "Romieu",
              "horse_id": "hrs_41814570",
              "race": "racingtv.com Novice Stakes (GBB Race)",
              "race_id": "rac_11588772",
              "course": "Redcar",
              "course_id": "crs_1222",
              "distance_f": "8",
              "distance_y": "1759",
              "quote": "Romieu is a nice horse and we think a good bit of him. He's very grand and big, but impressive too. He didn't have to beat much, but there wasn't much more he could have done. He's unexposed and it'll be interesting to see what the handicapper does with him, but we're hoping to be aiming for a nice prize at the Dante meeting next - Adrian Keatley, trainer."
            }
          ],
