          "comment": "Course winner but yet to threaten this season and a major turnaround is required",
          "spotlight": "Has often run well here and he won twice last year (1m5f/1m4f); however, he's failed to threaten on his three starts this season, here the last twice, and a major turnaround is required.",
          "quotes": [
            {
              "date": "2024-06-02",
              "horse": "Dark Moon Rising",
              "horse_id": "hrs_24867899",
              "race": "Sky Bet Club Handicap",
              "race_id": "rac_11270168",
              "course": "Hamilton",
              "course_id": "crs_572",
              "distance_f": "13",
              "distance_y": "2876",
              "quote": "Dark Moon Rising is a talented horse when he's on a good day. He was very well handicapped on his old form. I don't know what was up with him, he hasn't been performing. But he travelled really strongly and galloped all the way to the line. He won cosily - Shane Gray, rider, talking to ITV."
            },
            {
              "date": "2021-06-22",
              "horse": "Dark Moon Rising",
              "horse_id": "hrs_24867899",
              "race": "Pure Broadband EBF Maiden Stakes (GBB Race)",
              "race_id": "rac_10217740",
              "course": "Beverley",
              "course_id": "crs_156",
              "distance_f": "7.5",
              "distance_y": "1636",
              "quote": "Dark Moon Rising is a work in progress, he was very green first time. I thought he'd be a bit wiser today but he was green again. But once he passed one he picked the bridle up and he travelled well into the race. He came good from two down, he knuckled down and galloped through the line well. He'll keep improving with racing. He's a big, laid back horse at home, he's just going to have to learn with racing - Kevin Ryan, trainer."
            }
          ],
          "stable_tour": [
            {
              "quote": "He had some high-class form at three and if he can revert to the form he showed in the Dante he's on a very fair mark and could be a nice horse for handicaps. I think ten furlongs is his best trip and he'll benefit from getting back on a conventional track after not handling Pontefract last time. We retain a lot of faith in him. 03-05-23"
            }
          ],
