          "comment": "Progressive 3yo who was strong at the finish for 1m win here last time; tops the list",
          "spotlight": "Got off the mark at the sixth attempt in Leicester maiden (1m, good to firm) last month and followed up on handicap debut here (1m, good) a fortnight ago; there are mixed messages from his pedigree regarding the step up in trip and he could do with settling better than last time, but this progressive 3yo was strong at the finish and could take a 5lb penalty in his stride for a top trainer who has won this three times since 2011.",
          "quotes": [
            {
              "date": "2025-06-28",
              "horse": "Archivist",
              "horse_id": "hrs_42452081",
              "race": "Al Basti Equiworld Dubai Mile Handicap",
              "race_id": "rac_11652875",
              "course": "York",
              "course_id": "crs_2782",
              "distance_f": "8",
              "distance_y": "1732",
              "quote": "I don't think the slow early pace suited Archivist that well and it took him a while to get going. He wandered about and he's still a work in progress, but improving with every run. There's a bit more to come and he could make into a really nice four-year-old. The John Smith's Cup may come too soon, and we possibly may be better to stick at a mile. A strong mile may be better for him, even though Tom took a while to pull him up. A stronger pace may see him to better effect - Maureen Haggas, assistant trainer."
            }
          ],
