          "damsire_region": "IRE",
          "trainer": "K R Burke",
          "trainer_id": "trn_45171",
          "trainer_location": "Coverham, North Yorkshire",
          "trainer_14_days": {
            "runs": "44",
            "wins": "8",
            "percent": "18"
          },
          "owner": "Nick Bradley Racing 33, Burke & Partner",
          "owner_id": "own_1370928",
          "prev_trainers": [],
          "prev_owners": [
            {
              "owner": "Nick Bradley Racing 33 + Burke",
              "owner_id": "own_1221792",
              "change_date": "2024-03-28"
            }
          ],
          "comment": "Two Listed wins this year, most recently over C&D four weeks ago; leading claims",
          "spotlight": "Hugely admirable 6yo who was second in this last year and has won two Listed races this year, most recently making all in fine style over C&D (good to firm) four weeks ago; has won three Group races in his career; should take plenty of beating.",
          "quotes": [
            {
              "date": "2025-06-14",
              "horse": "Al Qareem",
              "horse_id": "hrs_27711383",
              "race": "Sky Bet Race To The Ebor Grand Cup Stakes (Listed Race)",
              "race_id": "rac_11637548",
              "course": "York",
              "course_id": "crs_2782",
              "distance_f": "14",
              "distance_y": "3048",
              "quote": "Al Qareem is so honest and brave, and very sound. He just does it every time you ask him to. Even when the favourite came looming up, I had a little smile on my face when the commentator said he was coming at him as you know he's going to lengthen and keep finding. The Ebor I think he'd be handicapped out of it, but the Irish St Leger looks a perfect race for him. It's a lovely, big galloping track and stays the trip so well. There and the Curragh Cup are likely to be the next two races for him - Karl Burke, trainer."
            },
            {
              "date": "2025-04-09",
              "horse": "Al Qareem",
              "horse_id": "hrs_27711383",
              "race": "Barry Hills Further Flight Stakes (Listed Race)",
              "race_id": "rac_11574238",
              "course": "Nottingham",
              "course_id": "crs_1040",
              "distance_f": "14",
              "distance_y": "3080",
              "quote": "The ground, I felt like Al Qareem probably just got away with it today. All he does is gallop when you let him down - Clifford Lee, jockey."
            },
            {
              "date": "2024-10-05",
              "horse": "Al Qareem",
              "horse_id": "hrs_27711383",
              "race": "BetMGM Cumberland Lodge Stakes (Group 3)",
              "race_id": "rac_11386245",
              "course": "Ascot",
              "course_id": "crs_52",
              "distance_f": "12",
              "distance_y": "2631",
              "quote": "I tried not to fire Al Qareem out of the gates, but he naturally jumps quickly anyway and going into the first bend he was half taking me on. I've got a lot of confidence in him and the petrol gauge never really fades. He just keeps galloping. He tries so hard and you know he's going to give you 150%. Even on the wrong ground he finishes on the backsides of the leaders, but he loves it when the going gets soft - Clifford Lee, jockey"
            },
            {
              "date": "2024-09-14",
              "horse": "Al Qareem",
              "horse_id": "hrs_27711383",
              "race": "Virgin Bet Stand Cup Stakes (Listed Race)",
              "race_id": "rac_11372348",
              "course": "Chester",
              "course_id": "crs_338",
              "distance_f": "12.5",
              "distance_y": "2703",
              "quote": "Al Qarem ran really well and he's a great horse to own. Every time you think you're going to have a quiet spell, up he pops and he puts a smile on our faces. We had him in the Irish St Leger and at various times during this week I thought we were going to run in Ireland, but I'm happy with the decision to run here. We're planning to run him twice again this season and he has options at Newmarket in a couple of Listed races and then we'll look at something else - Nick Bradley, part-owner."
            },
            {
              "date": "2023-10-07",
              "horse": "Al Qareem",
              "horse_id": "hrs_27711383",
              "race": "Jim Barry Cumberland Lodge Stakes (Group 3)",
              "race_id": "rac_11032424",
              "course": "Ascot",
              "course_id": "crs_52",
              "distance_f": "12",
              "distance_y": "2631",
              "quote": "All Al Qareem does is gallop and he loves these stiff finishes. I always thought I was going to get back up because my lad tries hard and keeps going - Clifford Lee, jockey."
            },
            {
              "date": "2023-09-16",
              "horse": "Al Qareem",
              "horse_id": "hrs_27711383",
              "race": "tote Stand Cup Stakes (Listed Race)",
              "race_id": "rac_11019996",
              "course": "Chester",
              "course_id": "crs_338",
              "distance_f": "12.5",
              "distance_y": "2703",
              "quote": "Everything went right and Sam James gave Al Qareem a great ride. I thought we were overpriced but you never know coming off a break like that how they're going to run. He picked up an illness when flying from Dubai which hit him pretty hard. We thought we might not get him back on the track this year but Karl has done a brilliant job - Nick Bradley, syndicate manager."
            },
            {
              "date": "2022-04-06",
              "horse": "Al Qareem",
              "horse_id": "hrs_27711383",
              "race": "racingtv.com Handicap",
              "race_id": "rac_10483629",
              "course": "Nottingham",
              "course_id": "crs_1040",
              "distance_f": "10",
              "distance_y": "2250",
              "quote": "We thought Al Qareem would win and he's been crying out for a step up in trip. He'll come into his own this season and the form of his Kempton fourth last year has worked out amazingly - Nick Bradley, managing director of owners."
            }
          ],
          "stable_tour": [
            {
              "quote": "He probably bumped into a good one [Internaute] on his comeback at Saint-Cloud but showed all his battling qualities to win at Nottingham on Wednesday. I don't think he really sees out the two miles like a strong stayer but he definitely needs soft or heavy ground over a mile and a half, and the Ormonde at Chester's May meeting looks the obvious next step. 11-04-25"
            },
            {
              "quote": "He was a huge improver last year with his handicap mark shooting up from 81 to 112 (31lb), which included victory in the Group 2 Prix Chaudenay (1m7f) under a cracking ride from Ryan Moore. We took him to Riyadh and Meydan earlier this year but he disappointed and I don't think the travelling suited him. He is having a break now and will be back for the second half of the season with the Ebor a likely target. 07-05-23"
            }
          ],
