          "damsire": "Medaglia d'Oro",
          "damsire_id": "dsi_3930262",
          "damsire_region": "USA",
          "trainer": "Brian Ellison",
          "trainer_id": "trn_39879",
          "trainer_location": "Norton, N Yorks",
          "trainer_14_days": {
            "runs": "16",
            "wins": "0",
            "percent": "0"
          },
          "owner": "P Boyle",
          "owner_id": "own_1169496",
          "prev_trainers": [
            {
              "trainer": "David Simcock",
              "trainer_id": "trn_145287",
              "change_date": "2021-11-29"
            }
          ],
          "prev_owners": [
            {
              "owner": "Never Say Die Partnership",
              "owner_id": "own_961836",
              "change_date": "2021-11-29"
            }
          ],
          "comment": "Won two nice prizes in 2024; some fair form this year but needs to raise his game",
          "spotlight": "Won last season's Northumberland Plate (2m, AW) and also a Group 3 handicap in Australia (1m4f, good) last October; some fair efforts in Meydan earlier this year, and also in the Northumberland Plate a fortnight ago following a break, but he needs to raise his game to take this.",
          "quotes": [
            {
              "date": "2024-11-05",
              "horse": "Onesmoothoperator",
              "horse_id": "hrs_23970548",
              "race": "Lexus Melbourne Cup (Group 1 Handicap) (3yo+) (Turf)",
              "race_id": "rac_11391159",
              "course": "Flemington",
              "course_id": "crs_7722",
              "distance_f": "16",
              "distance_y": "3520",
              "quote": "Onesmoothoperator just got too far back and then got hampered turning in. Nothing really went right for him but that's racing. We've had a great trip still as he's won. The last week hasn't been great with him pulling his shoe off and you want to go into these races at 100 per cent. Even though he didn't miss a lot of work, if you get a cut it still causes some issues - Brian Ellison, trainer."
            },
            {
              "date": "2024-10-23",
              "horse": "Onesmoothoperator",
              "horse_id": "hrs_23970548",
              "race": "Ladbrokes Geelong Cup (Group 3 Handicap) (3yo+) (Turf)",
              "race_id": "rac_11438414",
              "course": "Geelong",
              "course_id": "crs_21372",
              "distance_f": "12",
              "distance_y": "2640",
              "quote": "I said to Craig [Williams] that Onesmoothoperator is not your normal stayer, he's got loads of speed and he's always had a good turn of foot. He gave him a great ride today and I think he's loved it here - he's been bouncing. He was too far back in the Ebor and nothing was coming from behind. The idea was to sit in the middle, but we got shuffled to the back and it was far too much to do. He still ran well and then we went to Kempton, but a mile and a half was too short because they went off slow. The winner has won a Group 1 and the horse behind us finished second in a Group 3, so the form has been really good - Brian Ellison, trainer, speaking to Racing.com."
            },
            {
              "date": "2024-06-29",
              "horse": "Onesmoothoperator",
              "horse_id": "hrs_23970548",
              "race": "Jenningsbet Northumberland Plate Handicap (Heritage Handicap)",
              "race_id": "rac_11270792",
              "course": "Newcastle (AW)",
              "course_id": "crs_35178",
              "distance_f": "16.5",
              "distance_y": "3576",
              "quote": "I've been wanting to win it for a long time and I knew I had Onesmoothoperator right. They went a hell of a gallop and, when he's like that, he's some animal. Turning in I said, 'This has hacked up' and Connor said he could have won on the bridle - Brian Ellison, trainer."
            },
            {
              "date": "2023-11-11",
              "horse": "Onesmoothoperator",
              "horse_id": "hrs_23970548",
              "race": "Virgin Bet November Handicap",
              "race_id": "rac_11101350",
              "course": "Newcastle (AW)",
              "course_id": "crs_35178",
              "distance_f": "12.5",
              "distance_y": "2738",
              "quote": "Onesmoothoperator wasn't even going to run until it was switched here, he was going to go to Sedgefield over hurdles. They switched it here and it's been a lucky race for me, I've won it three times. He needs a good gallop and he got a brilliant ride. Ben made his move round the top bend and had everything covered - and you have to come up this rail. He's a funny ride because you have to take your time and ride him for luck. It's more than likely that he'll still go hurdling. He's a brilliant jumper and the one time we ran him they walked round and it was no good to him - Brian Ellison, trainer."
            }
          ],
          "stable_tour": [
            {
              "quote": "If I've got a Northumberland Plate horse in the yard at this stage, it would be him. However, he's better over a mile and a half. He ran in the Plate two years ago and the surface was very deep, which is no good to him. It changes at Newcastle; when he won the November Handicap there it was riding quick. He ran well to finish second at Southwell last time. I love him - he turns up all the time. I think we'll go to Newcastle for all-weather finals day, probably for the mile-and-a-quarter race but he'll be in the two-mile race as well. There isn't a mile-and-a-half race then and we'll probably ride him a bit handier in the shorter race. He's in great form. He acts well on grass too as long as it's good ground. 03-04-24"
            }
          ],
