          "comment": "On a long losing run but unlucky at Haydock last week and too well treated to be ignored",
          "spotlight": "Decidedly useful at his peak, third in the 2023 Wokingham; slow to get going this year but he's very well handicapped as a result and he was arguably unlucky not to win when fifth at Haydock (repeatedly short of room) last week; can blow the start, so not one for maximum confidence, but he's too well treated to be ignored.",
          "quotes": [],
          "stable_tour": [
            {
              "quote": "He was bought by his owner out of a claimer at Redcar in the summer from Ed Dunlop, so I can't take any credit for such a smart purchase. He has been a joy to train and the improvement has been very swift, as having started off on 72, he's now up to 93 as we look forward to this year. He won three on the bounce for us but his last run when third in the Ayr Gold Cup was very smart form. He has really pleased me with how he's done over the winter and I'd like to think he hasn't hit the ceiling of his ability yet. He'll be aimed at the big 6f handicaps and the Ayr Gold Cup is likely to be his main target again. 22-03-23"
            }
          ],
