          "prev_trainers": [],
          "prev_owners": [],
          "comment": "Front-runner who made all in a big field over C&D in May; in the mix once more",
          "spotlight": "Front-runner who made all in a big field over C&D (good) in May and ran creditably when third at Doncaster in June; in the mix once more.",
          "quotes": [
            {
              "date": "2025-05-31",
              "horse": "Ingleby Archie",
              "horse_id": "hrs_36738653",
              "race": "William Hill Keep Your Raceday Positive Handicap",
              "race_id": "rac_11622689",
              "course": "York",
              "course_id": "crs_2782",
              "distance_f": "6",
              "distance_y": "1320",
              "quote": "I'm chuffed to bits. The horses are just starting to run well and it might not have been the best of races, but a winner is a winner at York. Ingleby Archie\\P toughed it out and Harrison is riding well. He's not the easiest as he can revved up. He completely blew out at Pontefract. I was sure the track would suit, but not walking across the Knavesmire. It was a 0-78, but the handicapper will definitely have a say as it was at York! - Adrian Nicholls, trainer."
            },
            {
              "date": "2024-07-17",
              "horse": "Ingleby Archie",
              "horse_id": "hrs_36738653",
              "race": "JW 4x4 Northallerton Handicap",
              "race_id": "rac_11325171",
              "course": "Thirsk",
              "course_id": "crs_2080",
              "distance_f": "5",
              "distance_y": "1100",
              "quote": "Ingleby Archie was getting warm in the saddling boxes and while it was humid in there I admitted to the owner it was a bit of a worry. On last year's form he looks quite well handicapped but it took a couple of runs to get going - Adrain Nicholls, trainer."
            }
          ],
          "stable_tour": [
            {
              "quote": "He won last time out at Redcar - it took me long enough to do it. He's a grand horse who finished second three times in a row. He got beat at 1-8 at Southwell on his comeback in February, but I don't have them tuned up in the winter so much. Hopefully he can come forward from his win as his form last year, when he kept knocking into one, was good. 26-07-24"
            }
          ],
