          "owner": "Frank Brady",
          "owner_id": "own_214592",
          "prev_trainers": [],
          "prev_owners": [],
          "comment": "Easy winner at Nottingham last week but this is warmer and his best form is at 5f",
          "spotlight": "Gained his fourth career win last week at Nottingham, sweeping through from the rear to beat four rivals comfortably; may have more in the tank but this is a warmer race and all his best efforts have come over 5f.",
          "quotes": [],
          "stable_tour": [
            {
              "quote": "He won for the first time at Bath on his most recent outing. We've had a few out of Frank's family; they're all late-maturing horses and he's exactly the same. He's just big and raw but the glimpses were there last year for everyone to see. The time before Bath he finished fifth at Beverley. Would he have won if he hadn't got stopped? I don't think he would but he would have been second to Yazaman. It looked like it would be proper soft ground at Bath but there wasn't as murain as was forecast, so it wasn't an excuse not to run him. We learned a lot from Bath. He was pretty raw, the track didn't suit, but he was well on top at the finish. The handicapper has put him up 11lb, whiI wasn't best pleased with, but it is what it is. I definitely wouldn't run him on fast ground and we'll mind him a bit this year, but he'll progress into a decent horse eventually. 28-06-24"
            }
          ],
