          "comment": "5-11 on AW; won in May and went close last time in a quality Curragh handicap; big player",
          "spotlight": "Good record at this track (5-11); won at Navan in May over 5f from a mark of 94; went close following that when 1l third in a premier Curragh handicap last time; wore first-time blinkers that day which are retained and he runs off the same mark; big player.",
          "quotes": [
            {
              "date": "2023-09-02",
              "horse": "The Highway Rat",
              "horse_id": "hrs_23324903",
              "race": "Rathkenny Handicap",
              "race_id": "rac_11030175",
              "course": "Navan",
              "course_id": "crs_5018",
              "distance_f": "5",
              "distance_y": "1100",
              "quote": "The Highway Rat was entitled to win a race like this on his AW form and he did. The second horse came to me and I had to keep him up to his work but I was always comfortable - Billy Lee, rider."
            },
            {
              "date": "2021-10-22",
              "horse": "The Highway Rat",
              "horse_id": "hrs_23324903",
              "race": "Al Basti Equiworld, Dubai Pat Smullen Mercury Stakes (Group 3)",
              "race_id": "rac_10336027",
              "course": "Dundalk (AW)",
              "course_id": "crs_29588",
              "distance_f": "5",
              "distance_y": "1100",
              "quote": "The Highway Rat is only a three-year-old and sprinters tend to improve. He's thriving so well at the moment and is a horse to look forward to. We still have to make our mind up whether we travel over the winter but he is certainly a horse we'll look forward to next year - Andy Oliver, trainer."
            }
          ],
          "stable_tour": [
            {
              "quote": "He'll probably come back for the Bold Lad Sprint Handicap on Sunday week at the Curragh. He hasn't run since May as he came out of Naas a bit jarred, which was unusual and disappointing. He's had his break since and is fresh and well. He looks to be fully himself. It's his first run back but he normally runs well fresh. We were going to run him this weekend at Navan but we decided we'd go straight for the Curragh. 11-09-24"
            }
          ],
